{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And he hastened.</b> The empty-headed say that Moses hastened when He mentioned forty, lest He say fifty. This is a great error, for reason cannot tolerate that he interrupt the words of HaShem while He was still speaking, for he would have been worthy of death at that moment. Rather, when the voice ceased, Moses immediately hastened to pray. Moreover, it is written thus in the Ten Commandments, and all Israel heard this; and how could it enter Moses' heart that the Holy One, blessed be He, would say fifty? And because He mentioned ונקה and לא ינקה, there was no need to say לשונאיו:" "<b>And the word ויקד.</b> From the proponents of the doubled [root], from the root קדקד, where 'their קדקד in the land' on the pattern of ויתם הכסף (Genesis 47:15). וַיִקְדוּ (above 4:31) is like וַיִּתְמוּ (Deuteronomy 34:8). Do not listen to those who invent roots from their own minds on account of the pattern, and in this manner they would liken כאבן (above 15:16)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {0 "The comment ends abruptly with an incomplete clause about לשונאיו; translated as the text stands."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:40:14.823133930Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}